---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "July 1, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Capital Swipe: Privacy Policy">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-16 sm:py-24 text-[--white]">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-block mb-10 text-sm text-[--white-icon] hover:text-[--sec] transition-colors"
    >
      ← Back to cristimilea.ro
    </a>

    <header class="mb-12 border-b border-[--white-icon-tr] pb-8">
      <p class="text-[--sec] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-3">
        Capital Swipe
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-[--white] mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[--white-icon] text-sm">
        Last updated: {lastUpdated}
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="space-y-12 leading-relaxed text-[--white]">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-lg text-[--white]">
          <strong class="text-[--sec]">Capital Swipe collects no personal
          data.</strong> It is a fully offline game. It has no user accounts, no
          ads, no analytics, and no third-party tracking. Nothing you do in the
          game is ever sent to us or to anyone else. It all stays on your
          device. This policy explains that in plain language.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Capital Swipe is a flag-and-capitals quiz game developed and published
          by Cristian Milea, an independent developer based in Romania. In this
          policy, “we,” “us,” and “our” refer to Cristian Milea, developer of
          Capital Swipe. If you have any questions, you can reach us at
          <a
            href="mailto:contact@cristimilea.ro"
            class="text-[--sec] underline underline-offset-4 hover:opacity-80"
            >contact@cristimilea.ro</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">
          Information we collect
        </h2>
        <p>
          <strong>None.</strong> Capital Swipe does not collect, store on any
          server, or transmit any personal information. We do not ask for your
          name, email address, phone number, location, contacts, photos, or any
          account login. We do not know who you are, and we have no way of
          identifying you.
        </p>
        <p>
          The game does save your progress (such as your scores, high scores,
          unlocked countries, diamonds, streaks, and settings), but this
          information is stored only <strong>locally on your device</strong>. It
          never leaves your phone or tablet, we cannot see it, and it is not
          linked to any identity. If you uninstall the app, this local data is
          removed with it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">
          How the game works offline
        </h2>
        <p>
          Capital Swipe runs entirely on your device. All of its content
          (countries, flags, and capitals) is built into the app when you
          install it. The game does not require an internet connection to play
          and does not send game data over the internet. Because there is no
          backend server and no account system, there is simply nothing for us
          to collect.
        </p>
        <p>
          Optionally, the app can show you a local daily reminder notification
          to nudge you to keep your streak going. If you allow notifications,
          these reminders are scheduled and shown entirely by your device. We do
          not use push servers or device tokens, and no information is sent to us
          or to anyone else. You can turn these reminders off at any time in your
          device settings, and the game works fully without them.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          There are none. Capital Swipe contains no advertising networks, no
          analytics or measurement tools, no crash-reporting services, no social
          media SDKs, and no other third-party trackers. We do not share, sell,
          or disclose any data, because we do not collect any in the first
          place.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Capital Swipe is family-friendly and suitable for players of all ages,
          including children. We have designed it with a simple, privacy-first
          approach: because the game collects no personal information from
          <em>anyone</em>, it collects no personal information from children
          either.
        </p>
        <p>
          This means the game does not knowingly collect, use, or disclose any
          personal information from children, and it contains no behavioral
          advertising and no data sharing. In line with the U.S. Children's
          Online Privacy Protection Act (COPPA), the EU General Data Protection
          Regulation as it applies to children (GDPR-K), the UK Age Appropriate
          Design Code (Children's Code), and similar age-appropriate design
          standards, there is no children's data to collect, retain, or delete.
          Since no personal information is collected, there is no data retention
          period, and no parental consent is required; there is simply nothing
          being gathered.
        </p>
        <p>
          Parents and guardians can let children play with confidence: the game
          is self-contained, works offline, shows no ads, and sends no
          information anywhere.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">
          App store privacy labels
        </h2>
        <p>
          This policy is consistent with the privacy information shown on the app
          stores. On Apple's App Store, Capital Swipe is listed as
          <strong>“Data Not Collected.”</strong> On Google Play, its Data Safety
          section reflects that no data is collected or shared, in keeping with
          Google Play's Families policy requirements for apps directed to a
          child audience.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">Data security</h2>
        <p>
          Because your game data stays on your own device and is never
          transmitted to us, it is protected by your device's own security. There
          is no online account to be breached and no server holding your
          information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">
          Your privacy rights (GDPR, CCPA/CPRA and others)
        </h2>
        <p>
          Privacy laws such as the EU/UK GDPR and the California Consumer Privacy
          Act (CCPA/CPRA) give people rights over their personal data, for
          example, the right to access, correct, or delete it, and the right not
          to have it sold or shared.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because Capital Swipe collects no personal data, there is no personal
          information for us to provide, correct, delete, or transfer, and we
          have no personal data to sell or share. <strong>We do not sell or share
          any personal information.</strong> You remain fully in control of the
          local game data on your device: you can reset your progress within the
          game or remove all of it at any time by uninstalling the app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">International users</h2>
        <p>
          Capital Swipe is available worldwide. Because no data is collected or
          transferred off your device, there are no international data transfers
          to worry about, wherever you play from.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          The current version of Capital Swipe is free and contains no in-app
          purchases. If optional in-app purchases are added in a future update,
          any payment would be handled directly by the Apple App Store or Google
          Play (not by us), and we would still not receive your payment details
          or other personal information. This policy would be updated before any
          such feature is introduced.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">
          Changes to this policy
        </h2>
        <p>
          If we ever change how the app handles data, we will update this policy
          and revise the “Last updated” date above. If a future change were to
          involve collecting any data, we would explain it clearly here before
          it takes effect.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[--sec]">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or about Capital
          Swipe, please contact:
        </p>
        <p>
          Cristian Milea, developer of Capital Swipe<br />
          <a
            href="mailto:contact@cristimilea.ro"
            class="text-[--sec] underline underline-offset-4 hover:opacity-80"
            >contact@cristimilea.ro</a
          >
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
